Abstract = {Cloud computing technology is widely used in the field of medical
   information, providing strong technical support for the information
   construction of medical and health institutions, but at the same time it
   also brings privacy disclosure of medical data and hidden dangers of
   medical information insecurity. Control is one of the key technologies
   in the privacy and security protection of medical data in cloud
   services. This paper aims at the limitations of the RBAC model applied
   to the SaaS model, improves it, and proposes a Service-Oriented
   Multi-tenant Access Control (SMTAC) strategy to meet the needs of the
   software rental service to provide security for multiple healthcare
   organizations in the region at the SaaS model.},
