Year = {2018},
Pages = {126-132},
Note = {4th IEEE International Conference on Big Data Security on Cloud
   (BigDataSecurity) / 4th IEEE International Conference on High
   Performance and Smart Computing (HPSC) / 3rd IEEE International
   Conference on Intelligent Data and Security (IDS), Omaha, NE, MAY 03-05,
   2018},
Abstract = {The broad implementation of cloud computing and Internet-of-Things (IoT)
   is driving current networking control system towards an advanced level.
   Mobile computing further increases the complexity of the deployment.
   However, the complicated system also has brought more privacy issues
   into the field. One of the problems of obstructing mobile apps is that
   contemporary coarse-grained access control embedded in the operating
   system provides limited privacy protections. As an emerging technique,
   edge computing is an alternative for speeding up manipulations and tying
   up the connected devices via the enhanced utilization of the computing
   resource and the strengthened flexibility/ability of the control. In
   this paper, we propose a novel privacy-preserving approach that uses a
   multi-layer access control in edge computing to enhance the level of the
   privacy protection. Our approach models a hierarchical classification
   deriving from the protection objectives. Experiment evaluations
   accomplished by this work also provide evidence for demonstrating the
   adaptability of our approach.},
