   AND INFORMATICS (ICACCI)},
Year = {2018},
Pages = {2270-2275},
Note = {7th International Conference on Computing, Communications and
   Informatics (ICACCI), Bangalore, INDIA, SEP 19-22, 2018},
Abstract = {Cloud Computing is an emerging technology in the present day scenario.
   Services are offered to the users based on their requirement through the
   use of virtualization. When a user requests for a service, Virtual
   Machine(VM) is deployed to leverage the service on a particular host. In
   order to maintain normal load and avoid overloading of servers, load
   balancing is required. For load balancing the VMs are migrated to
   lightly loaded secured host. In order to migrate to the host security of
   the VM has to be taken care. Security is provided using software defined
   networks(SDN). In this paper VM migration is carried out using SDN
   controller. SDN controller maintains access control list of hosts and
   resource availability. Based on the two parameters mentioned VMs are
   migrated to another host. Security parameters such as data integrity,
   confidentiality is obtained to the user.},
