Note = {13th International Conference on Network and System Security (NSS),
   Sapporo, JAPAN, DEC 15-18, 2019},
Abstract = {With the rapid development of cloud computing technology, more and more
   users save a large amount of data in cloud storage. In addition to
   meeting the performance requirements, how to ensure the integrity of
   these data has become a hot topic for academic research in recent years.
   Provable data possession (PDP) based on trusted party auditor (TPA) is
   an important method to solve this problem. Decentralized storage based
   on blockchain technology, which has emerged in recent years, can well
   realize the proof of data possession. But it can't seamlessly interface
   with high-performance cloud storage. In this paper, we propose a PDP
   model based on blockchain and TPA (BT-PDP). On this basis, a distributed
   secure file system (FS) is implemented to realize a BT-PDP proof of
   massive electronic data.},
